# Facts of the guard set that stands between a wire command and its execution. site = which of the three hand-written copies is judged:
# top = C# CommandRouter.CheckGuards, batch = the per-line guards of C# BatchHelper.Execute, py = Python middleware (check_read_only, check_play_mode_required) + server._send_raw.
# mutating is the output of isMutating (mutability.logic) for the same call: the host passes it in (site py asks with unknown_is_write=true, top and batch with false). allowedInPlay is the host's allow-list
# (IsAllowedMutationInPlayMode plus the playOk registration flag of M3). A py caller fills the facts it does not own with the neutral value (readOnly=false, playKnown=false, pythonOnly=false) and acts on the verdicts it owns.
CONTRACT unitymcp.guards
COVERAGE declared-scope
MODULE guard_facts
FACT guard.site enum=top,batch,py closed
FACT guard.ready bool
FACT guard.batchable bool
FACT guard.pythonOnly bool
FACT guard.authDenied bool
FACT guard.compiling bool
FACT guard.allowedDuringCompile bool
FACT guard.playMode bool
FACT guard.playKnown bool
FACT guard.mutating bool
FACT guard.allowedInPlay bool
FACT guard.runtime bool
FACT guard.readOnly bool
FACT guard.alwaysAllowed bool
FACT guard.toolEnabled bool
INPUT guardVerdict guard.site guard.ready guard.batchable guard.pythonOnly guard.authDenied guard.compiling guard.allowedDuringCompile guard.playMode guard.playKnown guard.mutating guard.allowedInPlay guard.runtime guard.readOnly guard.alwaysAllowed guard.toolEnabled
